@host = http://localhost:5217

### 1. Status (publico)
GET {{host}}/status
Accept: application/json

### 2. Cadastro (publico) -> 201, sempre com role CLIENT
# @name register
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Daniel",
  "email": "daniel@veyra.local",
  "password": "senha@12345"
}

### 3. Login (publico) -> 200 com accessToken + refreshToken
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "daniel@veyra.local",
  "password": "senha@12345"
}

### 4. Sem token -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/users
Accept: application/json

### 5. Com token -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/users
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 6. Perfil do token atual
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 7. Delete com token de CLIENT -> 403
DELETE {{host}}/api/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 8. Login do admin semeado (Development)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@veyra.local",
  "password": "admin@12345"
}

### 9. Delete com token de ADMIN -> 204
DELETE {{host}}/api/users/2
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 10. Refresh -> 200, devolve um par novo e invalida o refresh usado
# @name refresh
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

### 11. Reuso do refresh antigo -> 401 e derruba a sessao inteira
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

### 12. Logout -> 204; refresh posterior devolve 401
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{refresh.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refresh.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}
